    a text called 'the length text' is 'gen extreme number'.
    a number called 'the length value' is 'the length text' as a number.
    a text called 'the buffer stem' is 'gen buffer name'.
    a text called 'the buffer name' is 'gen buffer reference' of 'the buffer stem'.
    a number called 'the buffer capacity' is 'rng below' of 32 add 8.
    a text called 'the buffer payload' is 'gen text payload'.
    a text called 'the list stem' is 'gen buffer name'.
    a text called 'the list name' is 'gen buffer reference' of 'the list stem'.
    a text called 'the list first' is 'gen extreme number'.
    a text called 'the list second' is 'gen extreme number'.
    a text called 'the list third' is 'gen extreme number'.
    a text called 'the buffer length subject' is 'gen buffer property' of 'the buffer stem' and "length".
    a text called 'the buffer size expression' is 'gen buffer property' of 'the buffer stem' and "size".
    a text called 'the buffer assertion' is 'gen assert number matches' of "KEY-54" and 'the buffer length subject' and 'the buffer size expression'.
    a text called 'the list length subject' is 'gen buffer property' of 'the list stem' and "length".
    a text called 'the list size expression' is 'gen buffer property' of 'the list stem' and "size".
    a text called 'the list assertion' is 'gen assert number matches' of "KEY-54" and 'the list length subject' and 'the list size expression'.
    a text called 'the length variable assertion' is 'gen assert number is' of "KEY-53" and "length" and 'the length value'.
    a list called 'the lines' is ["a number called length is {'the length text'}", "a buffer called {'the buffer name'} is {'the buffer capacity'} bytes in size", "append \"{'the buffer payload'}\" to {'the buffer name'}", 'the buffer assertion', "a list called {'the list name'} is [{'the list first'}, {'the list second'}, {'the list third'}]", 'the list assertion', 'the length variable assertion'].
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

(KEY-73 - LANGUAGE.md:5311-5312: `version` is contextual - claimed only
 in the `Library <name> version "..."` and `see <lib> version "..."`
 headers, an ordinary identifier everywhere else. Only the
 ordinary-identifier half is a leaf: the header half needs a second
 compilation unit and a built `.lib`, which no leaf produces today - the
 ledger's own KEY-73 row says so, and its retained probe carries only
 this half for the same reason. `version` is the contextual keyword
 itself, not a pool draw.)

To 'gen leaf contextual keyword version' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    a text called 'the version text' is 'gen extreme number'.
    a number called 'the version value' is 'the version text' as a number.
    a text called 'the assertion' is 'gen assert number is' of "KEY-73" and "version" and 'the version value'.
    a list called 'the lines' is ["a number called version is {'the version text'}", 'the assertion'].
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.
